| Command   | Use                                   | Example                             |
| --------- | ------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- |
| `pwd`     | Display the current working directory | `pwd`                               |
| `ls`      | List files and directories            | `ls -la`                            |
| `cd`      | Change the current directory          | `cd /var/log`                       |
| `mkdir`   | Create a new directory                | `mkdir project`                     |
| `rmdir`   | Remove an empty directory             | `rmdir test`                        |
| `touch`   | Create an empty file                  | `touch app.log`                     |
| `cat`     | Display file contents                 | `cat config.txt`                    |
| `less`    | View large files page by page         | `less /var/log/syslog`              |
| `head`    | Show the first lines of a file        | `head -10 file.txt`                 |
| `tail`    | Show the last lines of a file         | `tail -20 app.log`                  |
| `tail -f` | Monitor a log file in real time       | `tail -f /var/log/nginx/access.log` |
| `cp`      | Copy files or directories             | `cp file1.txt backup/`              |
| `mv`      | Move or rename files                  | `mv old.txt new.txt`                |
| `rm`      | Delete files                          | `rm file.txt`                       |
| `rm -rf`  | Delete a directory and its contents   | `rm -rf temp/`                      |
| `find`    | Search for files or directories       | `find / -name "*.log"`              |
| `grep`    | Search for text inside files          | `grep "ERROR" app.log`              |
| `sort`    | Sort file contents                    | `sort users.txt`                    |
| `uniq`    | Remove duplicate adjacent lines       | `sort users.txt \| uniq`            |
| `wc`      | Count lines, words, and characters    | `wc -l file.txt`                    |
| `echo`    | Print text or variables               | `echo $HOME`                        |
| `history` | Show previously executed commands     | `history`                           |
| `clear`   | Clear the terminal screen             | `clear`                             |
